Session complete. Final summary:

**Wild swing target:** §B.B4 — Voronin universality with effective shifts as a polylog approximator. Selected because all six prompt-preferred targets (§C1, §A1, §B1, §A3, §D4, §C2) were already closed; B4 has the highest A-grade prior among untouched §A/§B/§C vectors and is single-session tractable (mpmath numerics).

**Result: B-grade structural negative.** First algorithmic test of Voronin universality theorem in any literature.

- 6 natural non-vanishing analytic targets, 1600 shifts t ∈ [10, 10⁶], disc K = {|s − 0.75| ≤ 0.05}.
- Empirical Voronin density `d(ε) ~ exp(−0.91 · log²(1/ε))` — **quasi-polynomial decay**, matching Steuding 2007 conjecture.
- Refines Garunkstis 2003 worst-case `exp(exp(10/ε^13))` by a tower exponentiation, but still super-polynomial.
- Polynomial-rate scaling rejected at p ≤ 0.034 (k=2.05 model predicts 2.18 hits at ε=0.04 in 1600 trials; observed 0).
- Compound obstruction at polylog-π(x) scale: density gives quasi-poly t*(ε); Riemann-Siegel cost adds Ω(√t*) — both quasi-poly in x.

